      "problem": "$-{a}^{2}(2{a}^{4}-3{a}^{2}-6)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}^{2}(2{a}^{4}-3{a}^{2}-6) & = \\\\ (-{a}^{2})(2{a}^{4})+(-{a}^{2})(-3{a}^{2})+(-{a}^{2})(-6) & = \\\\ ((-1)\\cdot 2)({a}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{4})+((-1)\\cdot (-3))({a}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{2})+((-1)\\cdot (-6))({a}^{2}) & = \\\\ (-2){a}^{2+4}+(3){a}^{2+2}+(6){a}^{2} & = \\\\ -2{a}^{6}+3{a}^{4}+6{a}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
