      "problem": "$\\frac{x}{2}(6-10{x}^{3})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}(6-10{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (\\frac{x}{2})(6)+(\\frac{x}{2})(-10{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{2}x)(6)+(\\frac{1}{2}x)(-10{x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6)x+(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-10))(x\\cdot {x}^{3}) & = \\\\ (3)x+(-5)({x}^{1+3}) & = \\\\ 3x-5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
